import json
from pathlib import Path
from collections import Counter
B=Path('batches/final_batch_aws_devops.region.03_1')
plan=json.loads((B/'tile_plans.json').read_text())
screens=json.loads((B/'screens.json').read_text())
g=json.loads((B/'inputs/path_glossary_bundle.json').read_text())
bundles=g['bundles']; byid={b['context']['concept_id']:b for b in bundles}
registry=json.loads((B/'scenario_asset_registry.json').read_text()); assets={a['asset_id']:a for a in registry['assets']}
checks={}
def check(tile,step,prompt,good,bad1,why1,bad2,why2,hint):
 checks[f'aws_devops.tile.{tile}.{step}']=(prompt,[(good,True,'This follows the stated evidence and the taught verification rule.'),(bad1,False,why1),(bad2,False,why2)],hint)
check('032','s03','What does creating a Python virtual environment isolate?','The application’s Python interpreter context and installed packages.','The approved AWS profile and Region automatically.','Dependency isolation does not confirm AWS context; that is a separate check.','All host-wide Python packages for every application.','The isolated context is for the application, not a replacement for the host’s global environment.','Consider which context the application uses for its interpreter and dependencies.')
check('032','s04','A Unix operator has created ENV_DIR but has not activated it. Which sequence verifies environment-scoped dependencies and execution?','Activate with source ENV_DIR/bin/activate; install requirements with python -m pip install -r requirements.txt, inspect with python -m pip list, and use that interpreter for the supplied script.','Install requirements globally, then activate ENV_DIR only before running the script.','Installing before activation into the global context does not establish the supplied dependencies in the isolated environment.','Activate ENV_DIR, skip package inspection, and use the host interpreter for the script.','Dependencies must be inspected and the supplied script must use the environment’s interpreter.','Follow the interpreter context through installation, inspection and execution.')
check('032','s08','A bounded inventory call returns NextToken. Which interpretation and next step are correct?','--page-size controls service-call page size; retain NextToken and resume with --starting-token in the same explicit profile and Region to collect the remainder.','--page-size fixes the total output count, so the token can be discarded.','--page-size does not bound the total count, and a returned continuation must be retained.','--max-items changes only the service-call page size; start again without the token.','--max-items bounds output; restarting without the continuation does not resume the remainder.','Distinguish the size of a service request from a limit on collected output.')
check('034','s02','The expected result of an approved restart action is absent. What should the runbook tell the receiving operator?','Follow the stated failure-handling instructions, stop at the stated condition and escalate to the named recipient.','Retry or substitute actions until the service appears healthy.','The runbook must identify a bounded failure response, not introduce actions outside the established procedure.','Record only that the restart was attempted and leave the recipient unspecified.','An attempt does not replace failure handling, a stop condition or who takes over.','Look for a bounded handover when routine execution cannot continue.')
check('035','s03','Which inspection sequence gives Pod status, scheduling/runtime events and the intended container’s output?','kubectl get pod NAME; kubectl describe pod NAME; kubectl logs NAME -c CONTAINER.','kubectl get pod NAME alone.','Status alone omits the relevant events and container output.','kubectl logs NAME -c CONTAINER alone.','Container output alone omits the Pod status and described events.','Map each command to one kind of observation.')
check('036','s03','The intended RDS instance meets the supplied engine and status requirements. What still verifies application data?','Connect with the supplied endpoint, client and approved credentials, then compare the supplied query result with the expected data marker.','Treat the operational status as proof that the expected marker exists.','Instance status does not verify application data.','Check the status again and omit the query.','Repeated status inspection still does not compare the data marker.','Separate the instance check from the application-data check.')
check('036','s07','In a versioning-enabled bucket, an overwrite displaced the wanted version of releases/orders.zip. How is that selected prior version restored as current?','Copy the selected prior version to the same key, creating a new current version.','Permanently delete the selected prior version.','Deleting the desired version removes it rather than restoring its content.','Remove a delete marker even though this case is an overwrite with no delete marker.','Delete-marker removal undoes a simple deletion; this overwrite requires copying the selected prior version.','Distinguish restoring an overwrite from undoing a simple delete.')
check('036','s08','A simple delete created a delete marker for releases/orders.zip in a versioning-enabled bucket; prior versions remain. How is the preceding version exposed again?','Remove the delete marker.','Delete the preceding version by its version ID.','Deleting a specified version permanently removes the version needed for recovery.','Conclude that the simple delete permanently removed every prior version.','The described simple delete created a marker, not permanent removal of the prior versions.','Identify what now hides the preceding version.')
check('038','s03','An already-built image must be published to ECR. Which sequence authenticates Docker and pushes the tagged reference?','aws ecr get-login-password --region REGION | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin REGISTRY; tag as REGISTRY/REPOSITORY:TAG; docker push REGISTRY/REPOSITORY:TAG.','Tag the image, but omit Docker authentication and the push.','A local tag alone neither authenticates nor publishes the image.','Authenticate Docker, but use docker pull as the publication operation.','Pull retrieves an image; publication requires pushing the tagged reference.','Separate authentication, naming the publication reference and publication.')
check('038','s08','actions/download-artifact reports no upload SHA256 mismatch. Which additional evidence verifies provenance before deployment?','Run gh attestation verify on the extracted file for the intended repository and inspect its verified source revision and build workflow/run.','Treat the download digest check alone as verified source revision and build provenance.','The download check verifies upload integrity, not the verified attestation’s source and build linkage.','Inspect only the revision-based artifact name.','The name is not a substitute for verifying the file’s attestation and inspecting its source and build linkage.','Separate download integrity from verified provenance.')
check('040','s03','Template validation succeeds. What confirms the approved S3 declaration actually deployed?','Inspect stack events, outputs and the bucket’s live property against the declaration.','Stop at template validation.','Validation is not evidence that the declaration was deployed.','Read only the local template’s property value.','A local declaration does not confirm stack results or the live bucket property.','Look for both stack evidence and live resource evidence.')
check('041','s02','Which evidence verifies authorized runtime retrieval of the supplied managed secret?','The approved runtime identity has secretsmanager:GetSecretValue for the supplied secret and retrieves it using the supplied identifier.','A different identity can retrieve a different secret.','That observation does not verify the approved runtime identity and supplied secret.','The consumer has a secret copied into source code, without runtime retrieval.','A copied source value does not verify authorized GetSecretValue retrieval.','Track the approved identity, requested operation and supplied secret together.')
check('041','s03','The runtime consumer receives the retrieved secret. Which verification avoids persisting or exposing it?','Check the consumer’s safe success result without displaying the value or writing it into source code or logs.','Print the secret value in logs as proof.','Safe success must not expose the retrieved value in logs.','Write the value into source code so later runs can reuse it.','Runtime use must not persist the secret in source code.','Verify the consumer’s outcome rather than the sensitive value.')
check('042','s03','The delivery record identifies review handoff as the longest measured wait. Which proposal is evidence-backed and bounded?','Change only that handoff and name a measurable expected outcome for its waiting time.','Change every delivery stage without identifying which evidence supports each change.','The task calls for one bounded change addressing the supported bottleneck.','Choose an unrelated stage because it is easier to change.','Ease of change is not evidence that the selected stage is the bottleneck.','Connect one observation to one bounded change and a measurable outcome.')
check('043','s03','AWS Config reports a resource noncompliant. The governing policy requires escalation before changes. What is the authorized next action?','Preserve the evaluation evidence and escalate through the policy’s stated path without changing the resource.','Declare an attack from the compliance result alone.','A compliance mismatch is not proof of an attack.','Apply a configuration change immediately despite the escalation requirement.','The next action must follow the governing policy, which has not authorized that change.','Keep the finding separate from the policy governing the response.')
check('044','s03','Completed drift detection reports a difference in a checked bucket property. What does this establish?','It reports that difference, does not repair it and does not establish correctness of unsupported or undeclared properties.','It repaired the bucket to the template value.','Drift detection reports differences without repairing them.','It proves every resource property is correct, including unsupported properties.','Unsupported or undeclared properties may not be checked.','Distinguish the comparison’s result from repair and exhaustive verification.')
check('044','s07','Two supplied update sequences finish with UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE and UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED respectively. Which interpretation is correct?','The first returned to the previous working stack state; the second requires resolving rollback failure before continuing.','Both statuses mean rollback completed successfully.','UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED is not completed rollback and requires resolution.','The completed status means the failed update’s desired change is now deployed.','Completed rollback indicates the previous working state, not success of the failed update.','Read the terminal status as a rollback outcome, not an update-success signal.')
check('046','s04','What verifies role identity and bounded permissions from the EC2 instance?','Use its role credential provider without embedded keys; check caller identity, then record a supplied allowed success and denied rejection under that role.','Use embedded keys and record only a successful operation.','Embedded keys do not verify the instance’s assigned role provider; one success also omits the denial check.','Check only that an IAM-role setting exists.','The setting alone omits caller identity and allowed/denied access outcomes.','Tie identity and both access outcomes to the same credential context.')
check('046','s07','With the supplied Pod Identity agent and supported SDK chain, what access comparison verifies the intended boundary?','The intended associated workload’s approved operation succeeds and the unassociated workload’s attempt is rejected.','Both workloads succeed, so association boundaries are verified.','Success from an unassociated workload does not demonstrate the required rejection.','Only the associated workload is tested.','That omits the unassociated workload’s required negative check.','Consider both the intended workload and the negative case.')
check('046','s12','Which GitHub OIDC setup and test verifies approved-workflow access while excluding an unapproved repository or branch?','Constrain aud and sub to the approved context, grant id-token: write, configure the credential action for the approved role, and verify approved success plus unapproved rejection.','Grant id-token: write, leave aud and sub unrestricted, and test only the approved workflow.','Token permission alone does not constrain role trust or demonstrate rejection of the unapproved case.','Restrict aud but allow any repository/branch and treat an unapproved success as acceptable.','The supplied repository/branch restriction and negative access test are required, not just the audience condition.','Review both trust claims and the contrasting workflow outcomes.')
check('046','s16','For a supplied operation, the role identity policy allows it but an applicable session policy does not; no resource-based grant exists and no other policy contributes an allow. What follows?','The identity-policy grant is limited by the intersection with the session policy, so this evidence does not permit the operation.','The role allow alone overrides the session policy.','Role identity-policy grants are intersected with any session policy.','A direct-session-ARN exception automatically applies even with no resource-based grant.','That exception concerns grants directly to the session ARN; this case explicitly has no resource-based grant.','Identify the source of the allow before applying the session-policy rule.')
check('050','s03','The supplied target is SNS. Which required authorization model should be selected for invocation?','Resource-based invocation permission scoped as supplied.','Assume every target must use an execution role.','SNS uses resource-based invocation permissions; not every target uses a role.','Change the event pattern instead of authorization.','The event pattern selects events and is separate from target invocation authority.','Use the model required by the target rather than a universal role assumption.')

# Authored, bounded inspection records. Placeholders name supplied approved contexts;
# no credential value, hash, cloud operation or runtime output is fabricated.
practice={}
def cases(n,prompt,hint,*items): practice[bundles[n]['context']['concept_id']]=(prompt,hint,items)
# Each item is a complete record or a bounded claim about a supplied excerpt.
cases(0,'Read each execution record and decide whether it meets isolated dependency setup, approved AWS context confirmation and supplied-script execution.','Track the interpreter and the order of checks; successful execution alone is not enough.',
('Unix record:\npython -m venv ENV_DIR\nsource ENV_DIR/bin/activate\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\npython -m pip list\nContext check: supplied approved AWS profile and Region match.\npython <supplied_script_filename>\nRecord: supplied outcome successful; ENV_DIR interpreter used throughout; global packages unchanged.',True,'The record shows activation, environment-scoped installation and inspection, separate AWS context confirmation and execution with that interpreter.'),
('Unix record: ENV_DIR created but inactive. requirements.txt installed with the host interpreter; packages listed globally. Approved AWS context confirmed. Script then runs with the host interpreter.\nConclusion: isolated execution verified.',False,'AWS context confirmation does not correct global installation and execution outside the isolated environment.'),
('Record: ENV_DIR active; dependencies installed and listed there; script runs successfully using ENV_DIR. Only afterward does the operator compare profile and Region with the approved credential configuration.\nConclusion: ready-before-run checks met.',False,'The approved profile and Region must be confirmed before AWS automation executes.'))
cases(1,'Read each inventory record and decide whether its full export and bounded continuation satisfy complete collection in the approved context.','Separate service-call sizing from total-output limits and follow every continuation.',
('Supported inventory command: explicit approved --profile and --region, --output json; neither --no-paginate nor --max-items on full export. Automatic collection completes.\nBounded exercise: --page-size controls service calls; --max-items bounds output. Each returned NextToken retained and passed as --starting-token on the next call with the same profile, Region and JSON format, until no continuation remains.',True,'Both full automatic collection and same-context manual continuation are present, with the two limits distinguished.'),
('Full export: explicit approved profile, Region, JSON, plus --no-paginate.\nBounded exercise: every NextToken retained and resumed in the same context.\nConclusion: full-listing and continuation requirements both met.',False,'Correct manual continuation does not fix disabling automatic pagination on the full-listing export.'),
('Full export: automatic pagination, explicit approved profile and Region, JSON, no output limit.\nBounded exercise: --max-items returns NextToken; operator discards it, claiming --page-size already fixed the total output count.',False,'The token is needed for resumption, and --page-size controls service-call size rather than total output.'))
cases(3,'Read the supplied Pod inspection excerpts and judge whether the diagnosis is supported by phase, relevant events and the intended container’s output without changing the workload.','Check which container produced the output and whether phase is being mistaken for health.',
('Supplied Pod and container names substituted in kubectl get pod NAME, kubectl describe pod NAME and kubectl logs NAME -c CONTAINER.\nPhase: Running. Runtime events: intended container repeatedly fails. Intended container output: supplied startup requirement missing.\nDiagnosis: the container startup failure is supported by events and its output despite Running. No workload change.',True,'The phase is recorded without treating it as container health; the relevant events and intended output support the startup failure.'),
('get: phase Running. describe: intended container repeatedly fails. logs for intended container: supplied startup requirement missing.\nDiagnosis: the Pod is healthy because Running proves every container is healthy. No workload change.',False,'Running alone is not a complete health diagnosis and the recorded events and output contradict this conclusion.'),
('get: phase Running. describe: intended container repeatedly fails. logs: output from a different container only.\nDiagnosis: the intended container’s output was verified and its startup failure explained.',False,'Output from a different container cannot serve as the intended container’s output.'))
cases(4,'Read each RDS verification record and decide whether it verifies both the intended instance and the supplied data marker separately.','Do not substitute operational status for the query comparison.',
('Identifier equals intended instance. Engine and status equal supplied requirements; endpoint recorded. Connection uses that endpoint, supplied client and approved credentials. Supplied query result equals the expected marker.\nReport: instance requirement met; data-marker check met.',True,'Instance identity, requirements and endpoint are recorded, and the query comparison independently verifies the marker.'),
('Identifier, engine, status and endpoint verified against the intended instance. No connection or query attempted.\nReport: instance requirement met; application marker verified by status.',False,'Instance status alone cannot verify the application marker.'),
('Engine and status meet requirements, but recorded identifier differs from the intended instance. Query against that other instance matches the expected marker.\nReport: intended instance and its data verified.',False,'The query result for another instance does not verify the intended instance.'))
cases(5,'Read each bucket protection record and decide whether it establishes the supplied recovery window for releases/orders.zip.','Check the lifecycle window as well as the versioning setting.',
('Bucket: versioning Enabled. Supplied lifecycle policy applied. Inspection: noncurrent-version expiration and all other applicable rules leave required versions recoverable for the supplied recovery window.\nConclusion: recovery-window requirement met.',True,'The record establishes both enabled versioning and lifecycle preservation of required versions.'),
('Bucket: versioning Enabled. Supplied lifecycle policy applied. Inspection: noncurrent-version expiration removes required versions before the supplied recovery window ends.\nConclusion: recovery-window requirement met because versioning is enabled.',False,'Enabled versioning does not override lifecycle removal before the required window.'),
('Bucket: versioning Enabled. Lifecycle policy applied; neither noncurrent-version expiration nor other applicable rules inspected.\nConclusion: required recovery window verified.',False,'Applying a policy without inspecting applicable expiration rules does not establish recoverability for the window.'))
cases(6,'Read each publisher/consumer record and decide whether the exact published ECR image and both approved access contexts are verified. DIGEST means the recorded publication digest, not a value to invent.','Track publication and retrieval separately, including the consumer’s reference.',
('Approved publisher: aws ecr get-login-password --region REGION | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin REGISTRY; tag already-built image REGISTRY/REPOSITORY:TAG; docker push REGISTRY/REPOSITORY:TAG succeeds. Publication digest recorded as DIGEST.\nSeparately prepared approved consumer: same Docker authentication for supplied registry/Region; docker pull REGISTRY/REPOSITORY@sha256:DIGEST succeeds. Retrieved digest equals publication digest; both identity-specific outcomes retained.',True,'Authentication, tagged push, recorded digest and separately authenticated consumer retrieval by that digest are all present.'),
('Approved publisher authenticates, tags and successfully pushes; publication digest recorded. Separately authenticated approved consumer successfully pulls REGISTRY/REPOSITORY:TAG; retrieved digest is not compared.\nConclusion: exact published digest retrieval verified.',False,'Tag retrieval without matching the recorded digest does not establish retrieval of the exact published image.'),
('Publisher authenticates, tags and pushes, and pulls its own publication by recorded digest. No separately prepared consumer authentication or pull recorded.\nConclusion: publisher and consumer access both verified.',False,'The publisher’s self-retrieval omits the separately prepared approved consumer access evidence.'))
cases(7,'Read each workflow/publication excerpt and decide whether it attests and immutably publishes the same supplied orders release for rev-42 with its traceability record. The supplied revision-based name is rev-42.','Compare the two file paths and look for all three retained publication references.',
('permissions:\n  id-token: write\n  contents: read\n  attestations: write\nsteps:\n  - uses: actions/attest@v4\n    with:\n      subject-path: releases/orders.zip\n  - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n    with:\n      path: releases/orders.zip\n      name: rev-42\nRecord: completed workflow attested and uploaded that file; workflow run, rev-42 artifact name and upload SHA256 digest retained together.',True,'The same file is attested and uploaded with the required permissions/actions, and run, name and immutable digest reference are retained.'),
('permissions: id-token: write; contents: read; attestations: write. actions/attest@v4 subject-path: releases/orders.zip. actions/upload-artifact@v4 path: a different supplied output; name: rev-42. Completed run retained with upload SHA256.\nConclusion: provenance and publication describe the same file.',False,'The attestation subject and uploaded file differ; retained metadata does not fix that mismatch.'),
('permissions: id-token: write; contents: read; attestations: write. actions/attest@v4 and actions/upload-artifact@v4 both target releases/orders.zip, upload name rev-42. Run completes. Publication record retains only rev-42, omitting workflow run and upload SHA256.\nConclusion: immutable content reference and build-run linkage retained.',False,'The required publication record needs the workflow run and upload SHA256 digest as well as the name.'))
cases(8,'Read each template/deployment review excerpt and decide whether the approved bucket change, references and deployment evidence are verified. Logical ID and property placeholders refer to the supplied values.','Validation and a local declaration do not replace live deployment verification.',
('Template review: Resources contains exactly one bucket at the supplied logical ID, Type: AWS::S3::Bucket; only the approved property and supplied references changed. Outputs use Ref on that logical ID.\naws cloudformation validate-template --template-body file://TEMPLATE: succeeds. Approved stack created from that template. Stack events confirm success; output equals deployed bucket name; live bucket property equals approved declaration.\nConclusion: approved deployment and Ref result verified.',True,'The record connects declaration, intended logical-ID references, validation, stack evidence and the live property; Ref yields the bucket name.'),
('Resources: supplied logical ID; Type: AWS::S3::Bucket; approved property declared. Outputs Ref a different logical ID. Validation fails on that reference; no approved stack creation.\nConclusion: references and approved change verified.',False,'The wrong logical-ID reference and failed validation do not meet the template/deployment requirement.'),
('Template declares the supplied AWS::S3::Bucket and correct Ref; validation succeeds; approved stack creation attempted. No events, outputs or live property inspected.\nConclusion: the approved change has been confirmed deployed.',False,'Validation and a creation attempt do not confirm deployed outputs or the live property.'))
cases(9,'Read the secret retrieval/use excerpts and decide whether each meets authorized runtime retrieval and safe consumption without value exposure or persistence.','Check identity and scope, then how success is reported.',
('Runtime identity: supplied approved identity. Permission: secretsmanager:GetSecretValue on supplied secret. Request: GetSecretValue with supplied identifier. Retrieved value passed directly to supplied runtime consumer. Safe result: success. Value neither displayed nor written to source code or logs.',True,'The approved identity retrieves the supplied secret and the consumer reports success without exposing or persisting the value.'),
('Approved runtime identity has GetSecretValue for supplied secret; retrieval and consumer use succeed. Logging records the retrieved value to prove success.\nConclusion: safe secret consumption verified.',False,'Logging the value violates safe consumption even when retrieval is authorized.'),
('Consumer succeeds using a value embedded in source code; no GetSecretValue request by the approved runtime identity.\nConclusion: authorized runtime retrieval and no persistence verified.',False,'The record uses a persisted source value and omits the required authorized runtime retrieval.'))
cases(11,'Read the compliance finding and proposed next-action records; decide whether each correctly identifies the mismatch and follows the supplied governing policy without inferring an attack.','Compare required and recorded values, then apply the policy’s permitted path.',
('Rule: supplied configuration rule. Noncompliant resource: intended supplied resource. Rule parameters require approved value; recorded resource configuration has a different value. Evaluation evidence retained with rule and resource. Governing policy: escalate to the established owner; no change authorized yet.\nDecision: record required versus observed value and escalate without change or attack claim.',True,'The affected resource, violated condition and preserved evidence support the policy-governed escalation.'),
('Same finding: intended resource recorded with value different from rule parameter; evidence retained. Policy requires escalation before changes.\nDecision: apply a repair immediately, then notify the owner.',False,'The supplied policy does not authorize a change before escalation.'),
('Same finding: noncompliant intended resource; required and recorded values differ. Policy requires escalation before changes.\nDecision: report that the evaluation proves an attack, without preserving the rule parameters or resource configuration.',False,'A compliance mismatch does not prove an attack, and the omitted evidence is needed to support the mismatch and next action.'))
cases(12,'Read the bucket drift excerpts and decide whether each conclusion stays within the completed detection evidence.','Look for the exact expected/current pair and the limits of the check.',
('Provisioning record identifies the supplied stack bucket. After supplied out-of-band change, detection completes. Stack resource and supported explicitly declared property recorded: expected declared value A, actual current value B.\nConclusion: this checked property differs; detection has not repaired it and does not establish correctness of unsupported or undeclared properties.',True,'The resource, completed check and expected/actual pair support only the bounded difference and stated limitations.'),
('Provisioned bucket; completed detection. Checked property expected A, actual B.\nConclusion: detection repaired B back to A.',False,'Detection reports differences without repair; the actual B observation does not establish restoration to A.'),
('Provisioned bucket; completed detection. Checked supported property expected A, actual B.\nConclusion: every unsupported and undeclared property is now verified correct.',False,'The supported explicitly declared property comparison does not establish correctness of unsupported or undeclared properties.'))
cases(13,'Read each stack event sequence and decide whether its failure analysis and rollback conclusion are supported.','Separate the first update failure from later rollback events and terminal status.',
('Initial stack: one EC2 instance provisioned. Controlled update: first failing resource event identifies the supplied EC2 resource and supplied failure reason. Later rollback events end UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE.\nReport: first failure/reason recorded separately; terminal status confirms return to the previous working stack state.',True,'The original update failure is separated from rollback evidence and COMPLETE is interpreted as return to the previous working state.'),
('Initial stack: one EC2 instance provisioned. First update failure and its reason recorded. Subsequent rollback events end UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED.\nReport: routine continuation stopped; resolve rollback failure through established guidance before continuing.',True,'FAILED requires rollback-failure resolution before continuation, not a completed-state claim.'),
('Initial stack: one EC2 instance provisioned. First update failure recorded; later rollback event fails and terminal status is UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED.\nReport: use the later rollback failure as the original update cause and proceed because rollback completed.',False,'The first update failure is distinct from the later rollback failure, and FAILED does not confirm completed rollback.'))
cases(14,'Read each EC2 identity/access record and decide whether it verifies the approved instance profile and bounded role access.','A success matters only when identity and credential context match the assigned role.',
('Instance IAM-role setting: approved instance profile containing one approved role. Role credential provider used; no embedded keys. Caller identity matches assigned role. Supplied allowed operation succeeds; supplied denied operation rejected. Both outcomes recorded beside assigned role context.',True,'Approved profile, one role, caller identity and both permission outcomes are verified without embedded keys.'),
('Approved profile containing one role is assigned, but script uses embedded keys for a different identity. Allowed operation succeeds; denied operation rejected.\nConclusion: assigned instance role’s permissions verified.',False,'The operations use a different credential identity, so they do not verify the assigned role provider or its permissions.'),
('Approved profile and role provider; caller identity matches. Both supplied allowed and supplied denied operations succeed.\nConclusion: bounded assigned-role access verified.',False,'The supplied denied operation must be rejected to demonstrate the required boundary.'))
cases(15,'Read each Pod Identity association and access-check record and decide whether it verifies both the supplied association scope and the intended access boundary.','Match cluster, namespace, service account and role before interpreting access outcomes.',
('Association: supplied cluster, namespace, service account and approved IAM role match. Intended workload serviceAccountName equals associated service account. Supplied agent and supported SDK chain used. Intended approved operation succeeds; unassociated workload attempt rejected. Each outcome retained beside workload identity and association scope.',True,'The association and intended service account match, and the positive and negative checks are recorded with their identities.'),
('Association matches supplied cluster, namespace, service account and role; intended workload uses it with supplied agent and SDK chain. Intended operation succeeds; unassociated workload also succeeds.\nConclusion: required associated/unassociated access boundary verified.',False,'The required negative case is not verified when the unassociated workload succeeds.'),
('Association belongs to a different namespace from the supplied namespace. Workload uses the supplied serviceAccountName. Only a successful access result is retained.\nConclusion: supplied association scope and both workload outcomes verified.',False,'The namespace does not match the supplied scope and the unassociated negative check is missing.'))
cases(16,'Read each GitHub OIDC trust/workflow test record and decide whether it verifies the approved role boundary without stored AWS keys.','Check audience restrictions independently of the repository/branch restriction.',
('GitHub token issuer configured as IAM OIDC provider. Role trust accepts only supplied approved aud and sub repository/branch. Workflow id-token: write; AWS credential action assumes approved role without stored AWS keys. Approved workflow gets temporary intended-role credentials; supplied unapproved repository/branch is rejected; separate wrong-audience case is rejected.',True,'Provider, both claim restrictions, workflow permission/action and all contrasting access cases verify the stated boundary.'),
('GitHub IAM OIDC provider and restricted sub; aud accepts any audience. Workflow has id-token: write and approved-role credential action; no stored keys. Approved workflow succeeds and unapproved branch rejected, but wrong audience also succeeds.\nConclusion: approved audience boundary separately verified.',False,'Rejecting the unapproved branch does not compensate for accepting an unapproved audience.'),
('GitHub OIDC provider and restricted aud; sub accepts any repository/branch. Approved workflow gets temporary role credentials without stored keys; supplied unapproved repository also succeeds.\nConclusion: approved repository/branch boundary verified.',False,'The required unapproved repository/branch case must be rejected.'))
cases(17,'Read each bounded STS request/credential or permission-evidence record. Decide whether its stated conclusion is supported. No credential values are shown.','First identify the grant source; distinguish a direct session-ARN grant from role identity grants and apply any explicit deny.',
('aws sts assume-role uses supplied approved --role-arn, --role-session-name and --duration-seconds. Returned access key ID, secret access key and session token all used with values concealed. Expiration and issued lifetime recorded and match approved duration.\nConclusion: bounded complete session configuration verified.',True,'The approved request, all three concealed credential fields and approved expiry/lifetime are present.'),
('Request matches approved role, session name and duration. Only access key ID and secret access key used; session token omitted. Expiration is not inspected.\nConclusion: complete temporary credentials and approved lifetime verified.',False,'Temporary credentials also require the session token; approved expiry must be inspected rather than assumed.'),
('Permission evidence: only role identity-based grant allows supplied operation; session policy does not allow it. No resource-based grant or other allow; no explicit deny.\nConclusion: this operation is not permitted by the role/session intersection.',True,'A role identity-based allow is limited by the session-policy intersection in this supplied case.'),
('Permission evidence: resource-based permission directly grants the supplied operation to the session ARN. Session policy does not allow it; no applicable explicit deny and no other limitations in supplied evidence.\nConclusion: this direct-session-ARN grant is not limited by that session policy.',True,'The direct-session-ARN exception must be preserved for this separately evaluated resource-based grant.'),
('Permission evidence: resource-based grant directly to session ARN allows operation; an applicable policy explicitly denies that same operation.\nConclusion: the direct-session-ARN exception means the operation is allowed despite the deny.',False,'An applicable explicit deny overrides the allow, including a direct-session-ARN grant.'))
cases(18,'Read each target-authorization excerpt and decide whether it uses the supplied target’s required model and only the approved action/resource, leaving event matching unchanged.','Review matching separately from execution authority, then choose the model required by the target.',
('Supplied role-based target. Trust: events.amazonaws.com may assume execution role. Role permissions allow only supplied approved target operation on supplied resource. Authorization record retains that scope. Event pattern unchanged.\nConclusion: required bounded execution authority configured.',True,'The record has the required EventBridge trust and scoped operation/resource permission without changing event selection.'),
('Supplied SNS target. Resource-based invocation permission permits only supplied bounded action on supplied resource in the supplied approved context. Event pattern unchanged.\nConclusion: required target authorization model used.',True,'SNS uses the required resource-based invocation model, scoped to the supplied action and resource.'),
('Supplied Lambda target. No resource-based invocation permission. Only the event pattern is broadened.\nConclusion: target invocation authority configured.',False,'Changing matching does not grant invocation authority, and Lambda requires the supplied resource-based permission.'),
('Supplied role-based target. Trust allows events.amazonaws.com, but operation permissions allow every action on every resource rather than only the supplied action/resource. Event pattern unchanged.\nConclusion: least-privilege bounded execution authority configured.',False,'Correct trust does not compensate for permissions broader than the supplied action and resource.'))

out={'schema_version':plan['schema_version'],'kind':'interactions_part','path_id':plan['path_id'],'batch_id':plan['batch_id'],'tiles':[]}
for tile in plan['tiles']:
 st=next(t for t in screens['tiles'] if t['tile_id']==tile['tile_id'])
 target={'tile_id':tile['tile_id'],'interactions':[]}; seen=set()
 isteps=[s for s in tile['steps'] if s['type'] in ('check','hands_on')]
 for pos,s in enumerate(isteps):
  cid=s['concept_ids'][0]; b=byid[cid]
  measures=[]
  for a in s['anchors']:
   if '#assessment:' in a:
    c,cap=a.split('#assessment:'); anchor=next(x for x in byid[c]['assessment_anchors'] if x['capability']==cap)
    measures.append({'concept_id':c,'capability':cap,'fact_ids':anchor['fact_ids']})
  if not measures: # hands-on with practice-only anchor: apply its relevant glossary capabilities
   measures=[{'concept_id':cid,'capability':a['capability'],'fact_ids':a['fact_ids']} for a in b['assessment_anchors']]
  ix={'type':s['planned_interaction_type'],'interaction_id':'ix.'+s['step_id'],'difficulty':'intro' if pos==0 else ('stretch' if s['type']=='hands_on' and pos==len(isteps)-1 else 'core'),'grading_mode':'client','standalone':True,'anchors':s['anchors'],'measures':measures}
  if ix['type']=='choice':
   prompt,options,hint=checks[s['step_id']]
   # Rotate placements rather than making every correct answer first. Keys derive from the authored predicate.
   options=options[pos%len(options):]+options[:pos%len(options)]
   ix['public']={'prompt':prompt,'options':[{'option_id':f'o{i+1}','text':v[0]} for i,v in enumerate(options)],'selection':'single','shuffle':True}
   ix['grading']={'correct_option_ids':[f'o{i+1}' for i,v in enumerate(options) if v[1]],'option_feedback':{f'o{i+1}':{'message':v[2]} for i,v in enumerate(options)}}
   correct='Your choice follows the stated evidence and verification rule.'; incorrect='Recheck the evidence and the explanation for the selected option.'
  elif ix['type']=='classify':
   if cid==bundles[2]['context']['concept_id']:
    a=assets['ds.orders_restart_runbook']; names=[c['name'] for c in a['columns']]; rows=[dict(zip(names,r)) for r in a['rows']]
    pre='Outcome: '+rows[0]['outcome']+'\nPreconditions: '+rows[0]['preconditions']
    actions='\n'.join(f"Action {r['action_order']}: {r['approved_action']}\nExpected result: {r['expected_result']}\nFailure handling: {r['failure_handling']}" for r in rows)
    ending='\nStop: '+rows[0]['stop_condition']+'\nEscalate to: '+rows[0]['escalation_recipient']
    good=pre+'\n'+actions+ending
    items=[(good,True,'The complete excerpt preserves the supplied outcome, preconditions, ordered approved actions, checkable results and bounded failure/stop/escalation path.'),(pre+'\n'+actions+'\nFailure handover: use your judgement; no stop condition or recipient supplied.',False,'The handover lacks a stated stop condition and escalation recipient, so the receiving operator cannot identify who takes over.'),(pre+'\n'+actions+ending+'\nAdditional instruction: if the health result is absent, repeat the restart until healthy.',False,'Repeating the restart introduces an action outside the supplied procedure and contradicts the stated failure handling.')]
    prompt='Read these candidate orders restart runbooks and decide whether each is a usable handover under the supplied procedure. A usable handover retains preconditions, order, expected results and failure/stop/escalation instructions without adding recovery actions.'
    hint='Compare the candidate’s failure instructions with the established procedure, not just its happy path.'
   else: prompt,hint,items=practice[cid]
   pubitems=[{'item_id':f'i{i+1}','text':v[0]} for i,v in enumerate(items)]
   ix['public']={'prompt':prompt,'buckets':[{'bucket_id':'supported','label':'Meets the stated criterion / conclusion supported'},{'bucket_id':'unsupported','label':'Does not meet the criterion / conclusion unsupported'}],'items':pubitems}
   ix['grading']={'assignments':{f'i{i+1}':'supported' if v[1] else 'unsupported' for i,v in enumerate(items)},'item_feedback':{f'i{i+1}':{'message':v[2]} for i,v in enumerate(items)}}
   if cid==bundles[2]['context']['concept_id']:
    # Each candidate quotes the first supplied failure-handling cell verbatim;
    # the judgement also inspects the candidate's other sections and additions.
    for item in ix['public']['items']:
     item['source']={'asset_id':a['asset_id'],'row':{'where':{'action_order':rows[0]['action_order']},'occurrence':0},'column':'failure_handling'}
    role=next(c['semantic_role'] for c in a['columns'] if c['name']=='failure_handling')
    ix['grading']['role_map']={bucket['bucket_id']:role for bucket in ix['public']['buckets']}
   correct='Each judgement follows the supplied excerpt and the verification criterion.';incorrect='Check the evidence behind each conclusion; a partial success does not establish every required boundary.'
  else:
   assert ix['type']=='table_select'
   a=assets['ds.orders_review_handoff']; cols=[c['name'] for c in a['columns']]; rows=[dict(zip(cols,r)) for r in a['rows']]
   tasks=[];answers=[]
   # Derived cell predicates, including all three outcome comparisons with the same signal.
   for i,r in enumerate(rows):
    fields=['selected_bottleneck','bounded_change','success_signal','expected_outcome','baseline_minutes','after_change_minutes'] if i==0 else ['baseline_minutes','after_change_minutes']
    for field in fields:
     task_id=f't{len(tasks)+1}'
     ask={'selected_bottleneck':'the bottleneck supported by the longest measured wait','bounded_change':'the one bounded handoff change','success_signal':'the signal used for both observations','expected_outcome':'the intended direction without an invented target','baseline_minutes':'the baseline for that signal','after_change_minutes':'the after-change observation for that same signal'}[field]
     tasks.append({'task_id':task_id,'prompt':f"In case {r['case_id']}, select the cell containing {ask}.",'target_kind':'cell'})
     answers.append({'task_id':task_id,'row':{'where':{'case_id':r['case_id']},'occurrence':0},'column':field,'expect_value':r[field]})
   for outcome in ['improved','unchanged','worsened']:
    matches=[r for r in rows if ('improved' if r['after_change_minutes']<r['baseline_minutes'] else 'unchanged' if r['after_change_minutes']==r['baseline_minutes'] else 'worsened')==outcome]
    assert len(matches)==1
    task_id=f't{len(tasks)+1}'
    tasks.append({'task_id':task_id,'prompt':f'Select the row where the before/after comparison of the same waiting-time signal shows the intended outcome {outcome}. Lower waiting time is the stated intended direction.','target_kind':'row'})
    answers.append({'task_id':task_id,'row':{'where':{'case_id':matches[0]['case_id']},'occurrence':0}})
   ix['public']={'asset_ref':{'asset_id':a['asset_id'],'columns':cols},'tasks':tasks}
   ix['grading']={'answers':answers,'task_feedback':{t['task_id']:{'correct':'This matches the supplied evidence or computed before/after comparison.','incorrect':'Use the same signal and the intended direction; do not infer an improvement from the change alone.'} for t in tasks}}
   hint='Check what the signal measures and compare its two observations in the intended direction.';correct='The selected evidence and comparisons support the bounded handoff change without inventing a target.';incorrect='Recheck the supported bottleneck and compare the same waiting-time signal before and after.'
  ix['feedback']={'correct':{'message':correct},'incorrect':{'message':incorrect},'hints':[hint]}
  measuredfacts={m['concept_id']+'#'+f for m in measures for f in m['fact_ids']}
  rems=[r for r in st.get('remediation_steps',[]) if cid in r['concept_ids']]
  if rems:
   # Copy an existing target, preferring one that reteaches the measured facts.
   rem=max(rems,key=lambda r:(len(measuredfacts & set(r.get('lineage',{}).get('fact_ids',[]))), (1 if s['type']=='hands_on' else -1)*len(r.get('lineage',{}).get('fact_ids',[]))))
   ix['feedback']['remediation_step_id']=rem['step_id']
  seen.add(cid)
  target['interactions'].append({'step_id':s['step_id'],'interaction':ix})
 out['tiles'].append(target)
(B/'interactions.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2)+'\n')
